rs a single dropdown labeled `JURISDICTION:` bound to `filterState` with only 5 hardcoded states (`WI`, `IL`, `CA`, `NY`, `TX`). Both a dedicated `JURISDICTION:` selector (`All Jurisdictions (National Overview)`, `Jurisdiction A..D`) and a dedicated cascading `STATE:` selector (`All States (Overview)` + all 50 US states, DC, and territories), along with `filterJurisdiction` state in [`GraphSyncContext.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/frontend/src/context/GraphSyncContext.tsx), are missing.\n2. **Missing `jurisdiction_filter` \u0026 Unfiltered Subgraph in `GET /api/graph/topology` (`Requirement 5.2.1`, `Acceptance Criteria 2–5`):** [`get_graph_topology`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/api/routes.py#L84-L250) lacks a `jurisdiction_filter` parameter, returns all 4 jurisdictions and all 53 states unconditionally in `base_query`, does not filter `fee_query` to non-rural (`f.is_rural = false`) entries when `state_filter` is provided, and leaves `policy_keyword` unused.\n3. **Multi-State Anchor Extraction Failure in `EntityAnchorLinker` (`Requirement 5.3.2`):** [`_extract_state_anchor`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/graphrag/entity_linker.py#L351-L403) returns only a single `Optional[AnchorEntity]` and exits on the first matched state, dropping the second state in comparative queries like *\"Compare allowable rates for A6522 between California and New York.\"* Additionally, [`_extract_jurisdiction_anchors`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/graphrag/entity_linker.py#L231-L255) maps `\"cgs\"` only to `JURIS-DME-B` (omitting `JURIS-DME-C`) and `\"noridian\"` only to `JURIS-DME-A` (omitting `JURIS-DME-D`).\n4. **Cross-Jurisdiction Traversal `AttributeError` \u0026 Regional Lineage Gap in `TopologicalTraversalEngine` (`Requirement 5.3.1`, `Requirement 5.3.2`):** In [`_execute_multi_entity_traversal`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/graphrag/traversal.py#L350-L375), step 4 calls `.data()` on `allShortestPaths` and crashes at `for n in path.nodes:` (`AttributeError: 'list' object has no attribute 'nodes'`) when resolving `State(s) + HCPCSCode`. In [`_execute_single_general_traversal`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/graphrag/traversal.py#L262-L301), `.data()` strips `.type` and `.items()` from relationships `r`, producing `\"RELATED_TO\"` in `active_edge_keys` instead of `COVERS_STATE` / `APPLIES_TO_JURISDICTION` and stopping at 1 hop (`ChangeRequest`) without reaching `CoveragePolicy`.\n5. **Multi-State Fee Dropping in `GraphContextAssembler` \u0026 Transmittal Citation Guidance in `HuggingFaceSynthesizer` (`Requirement 5.3.1`, `Requirement 5.3.2`, `Acceptance Criterion 6`):** [`assemble_context`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/graphrag/context_assembler.py#L140-L160) picks only the first `A6522` fee via `next(...)` and skips all subsequent `A6522` entries (`if h_code != \"A6522\"`), dropping the second state's rate in cross-state comparisons. [`HuggingFaceSynthesizer`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/graphrag/synthesizer.py#L30-L39) does not explicitly require citing the governing `ChangeRequest` (`[CMS-CR-13286]`) and transmittal ID (`12349`) on regional/state administrative queries.\n6. **Territorial Jurisdiction Coverage \u0026 Contractor Naming (`Section 4`, `Requirement 5.1.2`):** [`DME_MAC_JURISDICTIONS`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/graph/tier4b_fee_schedule.py#L38-L78) and [`STATE_NAME_TO_CODE`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/src/graphrag/entity_linker.py#L15-L30) include 53 jurisdictions (50 US states + `DC`, `PR`, `VI`), omitting the 3 Pacific territories (`AS`, `GU`, `MP`) listed under `JURIS-DME-D` in Section 4 of `functional_specification_008.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Sufficiency \u0026 Scan Certification\nThe codebase dependency cone is exhaustively enumerated using verbatim symbols, all external schemas are grounded in observed empirical evidence saved in `assets/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/`, and all deficiencies are explicitly recorded without invention (`{sufficient}`).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Handoff Manifest Affirmation\n[`handoff/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/plan-scan-1.txt`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/handoff/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/plan-scan-1.txt) has been atomically overwritten with exclusively the 37 repository-relative paths of qualified codebase components, [`scan_reports/scan_report_008_plan_scan_1.md`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T185957-734-5ytd/scan_reports/scan_report_008_plan_scan_1.md), and the 9 captured payload files in `assets/20261013T185957-734-5ytd/`.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Coding Gate Affirmation\n**DO NOT CODE YET: Implementation coding gate remains locked. Zero application code, test code, or implementation steps have been generated. Coding waits on an empty frontier and explicit operator authorization.**\n\n\u003cpromise\u003eCOMPLETE\u003c/promise\u003e\n","duration_seconds":662.348826,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":249893,"output_tokens":52288,"thinking_tokens":14981,"cache_read_tokens":4434120,"total_tokens":302181}}}

